title: '2026-11-14: The switch of whose overrides a view follows is built, in all three clients, on main.'
pid: 7aa5ea57-0e54-4e8f-b6cf-521577bf98ed
body: |2-
  Jeff's request: a command that makes every node he overrides show his
  override in a buffer, the root author's overrides staying the default;
  it rerenders, and refuses a buffer with unsaved edits. Built as asked.
  What I learned about following is under "what I know", in "A view
  follows the overrides of its root's author, unless it is switched to
  follow the user's": its decisions and two consequences.
